<title>USA: Trans World Ent Q1 shr loss $0.09.</title>
<headline>Trans World Ent Q1 shr loss $0.09.</headline>
<dateline>ALBANY 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trans World Entertainment Corp</p>
<p>				   Financial Results</p>
<p>INCOME STATEMENTS:</p>
<p>(in thousands,</p>
<p>except per share data)</p>
<p>					    Thirteen Weeks Ended</p>
<p>				     May 3,     % to   May 4,    % to</p>
<p>					 1997    Sales     1996   Sales</p>
<p>Sales</p>
<p>				    $109,512	   $106,622</p>
<p> Cost of sales		    70,248   64.1%   69,453   65.1%</p>
<p> Gross profit		     39,264   35.9%   37,169   34.9%</p>
<p>Selling, general and</p>
<p>  administrative expenses     35,349   32.3%   34,697   32.5%</p>
<p>Depreciation and</p>
<p>  amortization		     3,586    3.3%    3,653    3.4%</p>
<p> Income (Loss) from operations   329    0.3%  (1,181)  (1.1%)</p>
<p> Interest expense		  1,742    1.6%    3,037    2.8%</p>
<p>Loss before income tax benefit</p>
<p>				     (1,413)  (1.3%)  (4,218)  (4.0%)</p>
<p> Income tax benefit		(551)  (0.5%)  (1,479)  (1.4%)</p>
<p> NET LOSS			   ( 862)  (0.8%)  ( 2,739) (2.6%)</p>
<p> NET LOSS PER SHARE	    ( 0.09)	    ( 0.28)</p>
<p>Weighted average number of</p>
<p>  common shares outstanding    9,770		9,734</p>
<p>SELECTED BALANCE SHEET CAPTIONS:</p>
<p>(in thousands, except store data)</p>
<p> Cash and cash equivalents    10,303	     50,655</p>
<p> Merchandise inventory	 159,699	    180,205</p>
<p> Fixed assets (net)	     62,958	     66,898</p>
<p> Accounts payable		 75,124	     78,826</p>
<p> Revolving line of credit	    0	     65,260</p>
<p>Long-term debt,</p>
<p>  less current portion	  48,176	     53,527</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity	  100,538	     91,424</p>
<p> Stores in operation		 478		  527</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
<p>NOTES: Trans World Entertainment Corp operated 748 retail</p>
<p>stores nationwide, including Record Town, Coconuts Music and</p>
<p>Movies, Saturday Matinee and F.Y.E.</p>
<p>Q1 results reflect sales from 49 fewer stores than year</p>
<p>ago, the company said.</p>
<p>Total Q1 sales up 3% from year ago.</p>
<p>Comparable store sales grew 5%.</p>
